# Clean Architecture Boundaries

- Keep routers thin: validate input, call one service method, return DTO response.
- Never place business logic, retries, or persistence code inside routers.
- Domain layer must stay framework-agnostic (no FastAPI, Beanie, Motor, HTTPX imports).
- Flow direction is strict: router -> service -> repository.
- Services orchestrate use cases and map external/infrastructure errors to app exceptions.
- Repositories only handle persistence concerns and return domain-friendly shapes.
